{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1029080-2e-wisdom-mortal-breaking-points","id":1029080,"title":"[2E] Wisdom & mortal Breaking Points","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Mage: The Awakening"],"posts":[{"date":"2017-01-09T08:22:25-08:00","id":1029080,"title":"[2E] Wisdom & mortal Breaking Points","content":"I want to add <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/806809-curios-relics-and-tomes\">Relics and Tomes</a> made by Mr. <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/775-reighnhell\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar775_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"775\" data-vbnamecard=\"775\">Reighnhell</a> to my games - I think that will add nicely too all the weirdness Mysterium is supposed to collect to Atheneum. Only thing is this - <b>Rules on activating those Relics most of the time are Integrity Breaking Points to various penalty levels.</b> How Integrity Breaking Points interacts with Widsom? Are they simply Acts of Hubris? If not, what is relation? And would mages activating Relics would roll over their Wisdom?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-09T08:41:30-08:00","id":1029090,"title":"","content":"If it's an AoH then they risk Wisdom, if it's not then they don't risk Wisdom to activate the item. It won't be a binary because sometimes things that threaten Integrity don't threaten Wisdom. What's the roll for activating the item if you have Integrity? Use the equivalent.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-09T16:28:21-08:00","id":1029326,"title":"","content":"The ideal solution would be separating breaking points and Acts of Hubris, so that while mages don't necessarily risk mental trauma from using magical items as part of the items' natural properties, they still risk spiritual degradation from using their powers irresponsibly.<br /> <br /> Maybe slap mages with the Guilty/Shaken/Spooked Condition as if they rolled a breaking point? I always imagined the key psychological difference of mortals and mages being that while both can be shocked by external factors, mortals are scarred and changed by it, but mages shrug it off as if it were a flesh wound.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-10T03:26:14-08:00","id":1029531,"title":"","content":"Mages can instant fix any non persistent psychological condition by throwing mana at it, so I assume that yeah, they can't be scarred that easily.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw","name":"WHW","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9102_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2542"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-10T03:29:27-08:00","id":1029534,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>WHW</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1029080-2e-wisdom-mortal-breaking-points?p=1029531#post1029531\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Mages can instant fix any non persistent psychological condition by throwing mana at it, so I assume that yeah, they can't be scarred that easily.</div> </div> </div> </div>Hmmm, are you thinking about Mind Arcanum? Or some general templates ability?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-10T03:35:19-08:00","id":1029537,"title":"","content":"Pattern Restoration.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw","name":"WHW","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9102_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2542"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-10T08:19:28-08:00","id":1029604,"title":"","content":"Okay, we can go with 'every time mage activates Relic, he just get connected Conditions and not roll on Breaking Points'. BUT there is other thing here - many ( like one tenth ) of <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/775-reighnhell\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar775_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"775\" data-vbnamecard=\"775\">Reighnhell</a>'s Relics have Soul Loss as effect on activation. Soul Loss in <b>Mage</b> is not so 'easy, peasy' to omit and he is not possible to Pattern Restoraition. How this would work on mage template and their Wisdom? Or maybe all Soul Loss effects should be changed in to something other when Relic is used by Awakened?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-10T08:40:49-08:00","id":1029611,"title":"","content":"You could still have it be soul loss, putting it back might be a challenge but that's not really a problem.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-11T00:14:14-08:00","id":1029950,"title":"","content":"<b>Reighnhell</b> have answered on the topics questions:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Reighnhell</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/806809-curios-relics-and-tomes?p=1029852#post1029852\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>Integrity Breaking Points</b><br /> When designing Relics, I leverage whether or not it causes a Breaking point as a cost-mitigating factor. I use it in cases where there is a particularly unsettling, soul-damaging or plain evil aspect of using the Relic. This goes above and beyond a Mortals typical response to interacting with the Supernatural. For a Mage, if the item triggers a breaking point at a 0 or -1 penalty, it is an <i>Understanding</i> Act of Hubris. If the item triggers a breaking point at a -2 or -3 penalty, it is an <i>Falling</i> Act of Hubris.<br /> <br /> <b>Soul Loss</b><br /> At the time I am writing this, I have created a total of 125 Relics - of these only two (<i>The Devil's Due</i> and <i>O\u2019Grady\u2019s Gloves) </i>have Soul Loss as a consequence of activation. A few others can inflict Soul Loss as one of its powers ( <i>The Harvester</i> and <i>Undying Love</i>). In either case, a Mage would treat this as they would any other hostile soul magic. While a Mage has access to powerful protective magic, without it they are as vulnerable to having their souls attacked as any Mortal. However a Mage is far more likely to know if a Relic has soul stealing powers, and they can decide well in advance if that is a cost they want to pay.</div> </div> </div> </div>Breaking Points seems okay, if we take them in context of 'truely evil items'.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}